;; The lock screen: the solo target for desktop/lock. A hidden system app — no launcher or dock
;; tile, reached only by locking. Locked mode fills the screen and refuses every exit, so only
;; the circle token stick or a peer's unlock releases it; unlock stops this app and goes back to
;; what was open. A GTK window, not a web app: locking must not cost a browser's worth of RAM at
;; the one moment the session is already full.
{:kind :exec :label "Locked" :category :system :hidden true
 :exec ["python3" "app/lock.py"]
 :window {:class "ujima-lock"}}   ; xprop-verify on HW
